From d61b2e186dfe61405368a925d9ea135b27683dde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:48:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] dos: Count repeated and unknown-previous-hop HSDir
 requests

Tor makes every anonymized directory request, including each onion
service descriptor fetch and upload, on its own circuit (ISO_STREAM in
directory_initiate_request()), and Arti uses a fresh circuit for each
HSDir request; both build those circuits through relays in the
consensus. Nothing counts how often an HSDir sees otherwise.

Count every anonymous onion service directory request, every repeat on
a circuit that already made one and each such circuit once, and every
request whose previous hop is neither in our consensus nor described by
a descriptor we have, as RefuseUnknownExits checks for exit streams.
Export them as tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_request_total",
"hsdir_req_reused", "hsdir_circ_reused", "hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}.
Nothing is refused. The cost is one known-relay lookup per such request
and two bits on or_circuit_t.

Part of #41339.
